  "cells": [
    {
      "id": "MJUe",
      "code_hash": "189a78ba0f77482b2b3a8cf758df56f9",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h1 id=\"query-rewrite-agent-for-improved-retrieval\">Query Rewrite Agent for Improved Retrieval</h1>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Goal:</strong> Build an LLM-powered agent to optimize queries before BM25 search, improving Recall@5 and MRR.</span>\n<h2 id=\"why-query-rewriting\">Why Query Rewriting?</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Your baseline BM25 achieved ~50% Recall@5. This means half the queries failed to find the correct recipe in the top 5!</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>The Problem:</strong>\nNatural language queries often don't match recipe text well:</span>\n<ul>\n<li>User: \"What air fryer settings for frozen chicken tenders?\"</li>\n<li>Recipe text: \"air fry at 400\u00b0F for 12 minutes\"</li>\n<li>BM25 issue: \"settings\" doesn't appear in recipe, query is too wordy</li>\n</ul>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>The Solution:</strong>\nUse an LLM to rewrite queries into better search terms:</span>\n<ul>\n<li>Rewritten: \"air fryer frozen chicken temperature time\"</li>\n<li>Better match: More keywords, less filler words!</li>\n</ul></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "vblA",
      "code_hash": "e0257cb437a851df716cae106beb2c61",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"prediction-question\">Prediction Question \ud83e\udd14</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Before we build the agent, predict:</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>How much improvement do you expect from query rewriting?</strong></span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Think about:</span>\n<ul>\n<li>Baseline Recall@5 was ~50%</li>\n<li>Query rewriting can help with vocabulary mismatch</li>\n<li>But it might also hurt by removing important context</li>\n</ul>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Predict new Recall@5:</strong> 65%</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Predict improvement:</strong> +15%</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">(We'll check your intuition against actual results!)</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "bkHC",
      "code_hash": "431d4df562655cb638feb122bf1632c6",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"three-query-rewrite-strategies\">Three Query Rewrite Strategies</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">We'll test three different approaches:</span>\n<h3 id=\"1-keywords-extraction\">1. <strong>Keywords Extraction</strong></h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Extract only the most important search terms</li>\n<li>Remove filler words (what, how, the)</li>\n<li>Focus on cooking methods, ingredients, equipment</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"2-query-rewriting\">2. <strong>Query Rewriting</strong></h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Rewrite the query to match recipe language</li>\n<li>Use terms that appear in recipe instructions</li>\n<li>Keep it concise but descriptive</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"3-query-expansion\">3. <strong>Query Expansion</strong></h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Add synonyms and related cooking terms</li>\n<li>Helps catch recipes using different terminology</li>\n<li>Example: \"bake\" \u2192 \"bake roast cook oven\"</li>\n</ul>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">We'll evaluate all three and pick the best one!</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "Xref",
      "code_hash": "3c298c4b817ab8ba7dcfae0685506c64",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"step-1-build-the-query-rewrite-agent\">Step 1: Build the Query Rewrite Agent</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Let's create a simple agent class with three rewrite strategies.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "BYtC",
      "code_hash": "981370663333ab1f7a9a1b28c0e99de7",
